cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use D'Agnese DIF-FNO or the D'Agnese Topological Barrier Loss, please cite it as below."
title: "D'Agnese DIF-FNO: Diffeomorphic Implicit Fourier Neural Operators with Topological Guarantees on Non-Convex Domains"
abstract: >-
  DIF-FNO is a Fourier Neural Operator preceded by a learnable, input-conditioned
  diffeomorphic coordinate map. Grid folding (non-positive Jacobian determinant)
  is discouraged by the D'Agnese softplus barrier loss and -- in the
  Lipschitz-constrained variant -- provably excluded by a spectral-norm
  certificate that guarantees det(J_phi) >= (1 - kappa*L)^2 > 0.
